{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '1,240p' openspec/changes/resilient-teardown-cleanup/specs/resilient-teardown-cleanup/spec.md && sed -n '1,240p' openspec/changes/resilient-teardown-cleanup/design.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Spec Delta\n\n## Purpose\n\nEnsure teardown cleanup is exhaustive and preserves every failure for callers\nafter request and application context state has been safely released.\n\n## ADDED Requirements\n\n### Requirement: Exhaustive teardown execution\nFlask MUST invoke every registered request teardown callback, application-context\nteardown callback, and receiver of each corresponding teardown signal, even if\none or more earlier teardown participants raise an exception. Flask MUST report\nthe collected teardown failure or failures only after the applicable context\nhas completed its cleanup and restored context-local state.\n\n#### Scenario: Request teardown has multiple failures\n- **WHEN** more than one request teardown participant raises while a request\n  context is popped\n- **THEN** all remaining request teardown participants run and the failures are\n  raised after cleanup finishes\n\n#### Scenario: Application-context teardown has multiple failures\n- **WHEN** more than one application-context teardown participant raises while\n  an application context is popped\n- **THEN** all remaining application-context teardown participants run,\n  context-local state is restored, and the failures are raised after cleanup\n  finishes\n\n### Requirement: Multiple teardown failure reporting\nOn Python versions with exception-group support, Flask MUST raise all collected\nteardown failures together in an exception group. On older supported Python\nversions, Flask MUST raise the first collected teardown failure after running\nall teardown participants.\n\n#### Scenario: Exception-group-capable runtime\n- **WHEN** teardown collects multiple failures on a runtime that supports\n  exception groups\n- **THEN** the raised exception contains every collected teardown failure\n# Design\n\n## Context\n\n`Flask.do_teardown_request` and `Flask.do_teardown_appcontext` currently call\ncallbacks and their teardown signals directly, so an exception prevents later\ncallbacks and receivers from running. `AppContext.pop` must reset its context\nvariable even when either teardown phase fails.\n\n## Goals / Non-Goals\n\n**Goals:**\n- Collect failures while continuing each teardown callback and signal receiver.\n- Reuse one small internal execution mechanism for both teardown paths.\n- Preserve existing callback ordering and exception arguments.\n- Raise collected failures only after context cleanup completes.\n\n**Non-Goals:**\n- Change teardown registration, ordering, or normal signal semantics.\n- Suppress teardown failures or alter exceptions from request dispatch.\n\n## Decisions\n\n- Represent teardown work as individual callables and execute it through a\n  shared internal helper that catches `BaseException`, records it, and raises\n  after all work has been attempted. This avoids duplicated, subtly divergent\n  request and app-context loops.\n- Dispatch signal receivers as individual teardown work items rather than\n  relying on a signal's bulk `send`, since bulk dispatch stops at a raising\n  receiver. Receiver lookup and invocation must preserve Flask's existing\n  sender and async-wrapper behavior.\n- Raise an exception group when the runtime provides it; otherwise raise the\n  first recorded failure. The helper returns only after all work ran, allowing\n  the existing `finally` in context popping to restore context-local state.\n\n## Risks / Trade-offs\n\n- [Signal receiver ordering differs from opaque signal bulk dispatch] → use the\n  signal library's established receiver iteration behavior and test that all\n  receivers run.\n- [A cleanup failure can mask an in-flight request exception] → this is the\n  settled teardown contract; retain the original exception as the `exc`\n  argument to every participant.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
